# Nothing in this directory reads a .env of its own. The real credentials for 04_vault_services.py
# are read, with a line parser (never `source`), from the file named by OSB_SECRETS_ENV
# (default ~/.config/opensandbox-eks/secrets.env). That file stays outside this repository. It needs:
#
#   GITHUB_TOKEN=        fine-grained token with push access to the private test repo below
#   GITHUB_REPO=         owner/name of that private test repo (a throwaway branch is pushed and deleted)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=   a key for api.anthropic.com
#
# Only those three names are read; every other line in that file is ignored.
# The CA trust, leak, substitution, rotation and pause tests (03, 05 to 08) use made-up dummy credentials against the
# in-cluster echo server and never touch these.
#
# Optional:
#   export OSB_SECRETS_ENV=/path/to/your/secrets.env
#
# The lifecycle server's API key (OSB_API_KEY) comes from ../opensandbox-eks/.env.
